[{:db/id "q-282168/field-1/ccb5b49a6a08ad746e85e4ebdcdb58d026eee15841c8bab991e7b32c0c3517dc" :answer/id #uuid "2e1393ae-93cc-522f-a225-ff5eba1e79fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5y^2-20y+65" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-282168/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e259043b-f98d-5de3-90d0-7adcd5da5b12" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-282168/field-1/ccb5b49a6a08ad746e85e4ebdcdb58d026eee15841c8bab991e7b32c0c3517dc" :answer-field/choices ["q-282168/field-1/ccb5b49a6a08ad746e85e4ebdcdb58d026eee15841c8bab991e7b32c0c3517dc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-282168" :question/id #uuid "69bfecff-a4c9-53af-810f-8c9439557c4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-282168" :question/problem "The quadratic polynomial $f(y)$ has real coefficients, has roots ${y}_{1}=2+3\\text{i}$ and ${y}_{2}=2-3\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $5.$ Find $f(y).$\n\n$f(y)=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots ${y}_{1}=2+3\\text{i}$ and ${y}_{2}=2-3\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=5,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(y-{y}_{1})(y-{y}_{2}) & =(5)(y-(2+3\\text{i}))(y-(2-3\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(y-(2+3\\text{i}))(y-(2-3\\text{i})) & =5({y}^{2}-(2+3\\text{i})y-(2-3\\text{i})y+(2+3\\text{i})(2-3\\text{i})) \\\\  & =5({y}^{2}-(2+3\\text{i}+2-3\\text{i})y+({2}^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2})) \\\\  & =5({y}^{2}-4y+(4+9)) \\\\  & =5({y}^{2}-4y+13) \\\\  & =5{y}^{2}-20y+65.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(y)=5{y}^{2}-20y+65.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-282168/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "70c149d8-3739-564c-97c5-6636860ad0c4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-282168"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-69563/selection/9109431868c63653c62184873cc4baaf76a72f95cc3ddf59001e5c745fa0ca8a" :answer/id #uuid "7d48c214-18a0-5b8b-8c83-f780b7a346bb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$7$ and $4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69563/selection/c76146d678198ccd365e62b6b9ed735becea953a6bc9e321da6a11c7de8c28df" :answer/id #uuid "4482e558-90fa-53b9-806a-8c75bac14a8a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$14\\sqrt{2}$ and $4\\sqrt{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69563/selection/9b510cdc82d8dad9bcbe86902f9b61aaa0961154a8f3ba1b576c96541928d96f" :answer/id #uuid "f9541b9f-c045-5de1-afc5-5387cd71f7a0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$14$ and $4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69563/selection/5c79f44b5e4fb7785dba1ca585e358d4e516396048ae0e38bee12b9ca70730fe" :answer/id #uuid "c5461de7-327c-52e0-b5c8-b080f14e4a23" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$7$ and $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69563/selection/3b3f3f5371c1c18e1006a37442ed96b1e53c0f06dad2a7701a7d3c442cdd3225" :answer/id #uuid "dac783cd-66d9-5e60-b99c-f692fb526bb9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$7\\sqrt{2}$ and $2\\sqrt{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69563/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "951051d0-8b82-59b1-84f1-e677f7e96b3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-69563/selection/9b510cdc82d8dad9bcbe86902f9b61aaa0961154a8f3ba1b576c96541928d96f" :answer-field/choices ["q-69563/selection/9109431868c63653c62184873cc4baaf76a72f95cc3ddf59001e5c745fa0ca8a" "q-69563/selection/c76146d678198ccd365e62b6b9ed735becea953a6bc9e321da6a11c7de8c28df" "q-69563/selection/9b510cdc82d8dad9bcbe86902f9b61aaa0961154a8f3ba1b576c96541928d96f" "q-69563/selection/5c79f44b5e4fb7785dba1ca585e358d4e516396048ae0e38bee12b9ca70730fe" "q-69563/selection/3b3f3f5371c1c18e1006a37442ed96b1e53c0f06dad2a7701a7d3c442cdd3225"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-69563" :question/id #uuid "8ca29321-6dcb-5eb2-8ac4-99202a87781f" :question/math-academy-id "q-69563" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=4$ and ${b}^{2}=49.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=4,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{4}=2.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=49,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{49}=7.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=7,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=2.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 7=14,$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 2=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-69563/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-69563"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-69940/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "af31d06a-cf3e-5b53-9d24-db0347176fe6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69940/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "c50fa07f-01f5-5330-a426-99614d47fbff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69940/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "3939d455-97d5-5fa1-a197-91a515d3a1a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69940/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "d01bb27d-91a7-5098-8f57-aa35b86d86d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69940/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "3bbeec9c-b1d3-59bd-9e76-516e2842f77e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69940/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "58b7b164-c435-5e81-af37-0d79f3949c95" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-69940/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-69940/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-69940/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-69940/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-69940/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-69940/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-69940" :question/id #uuid "0c794907-2a8c-5720-b1b4-1f1e6bf16096" :question/math-academy-id "q-69940" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\text{u}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $\\text{v}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 2-2\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-2+2 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|\\,0\\,|=0\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-69940/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0272b8d6-8400-5a6d-b51d-fc6ca84bd166"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-69940"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-337668/field-1/219833e72de92bafe4f4f5813822a337104a6b771fd9bf741ddcca8750ecab9e" :answer/id #uuid "e0f21b7e-5339-5b54-a9b8-41f04585b70e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337668/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a06c6805-870e-56ee-8e96-88e115ada4c7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-337668/field-1/219833e72de92bafe4f4f5813822a337104a6b771fd9bf741ddcca8750ecab9e" :answer-field/choices ["q-337668/field-1/219833e72de92bafe4f4f5813822a337104a6b771fd9bf741ddcca8750ecab9e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337668/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "0ce9bff4-1e58-5e5c-bfea-c5f84eea1f93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337668/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "b060abd8-45d0-5064-ad6b-483e0db53ed5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-337668/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-337668/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337668/field-3/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "0cd20774-9c5e-5470-9b57-386b0b0f1768" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337668/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "c6c8a442-9c73-567d-8c41-f7880e3cb806" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-337668/field-3/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-337668/field-3/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337668" :question/id #uuid "edafa2b5-0c55-598b-8ba1-9ebc55335790" :question/math-academy-id "q-337668" :question/problem "Find the product $AB$, if\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]$\nand \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & \\sqrt{3} & 5 \\\\ 4\\sqrt{2} & -1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & -3\\sqrt{5} & 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n| $AB=$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is the $2$nd *row* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $B$ by the $2$nd *row* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}$ on the *left*, the result must be the $2$nd *row* of $B.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nAB=[\\begin{aligned}4\\sqrt{2} & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nLet's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & \\sqrt{3} & 5 \\\\ 4\\sqrt{2} & -1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & -3\\sqrt{5} & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4\\sqrt{2} & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-337668/field-1" "q-337668/field-2" "q-337668/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89362140-1a17-56fd-a9ab-4da336112bee"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-337668"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123699/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "42ce795e-5972-57c4-80df-b3fe60008618" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123699/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "37df9160-b0e2-5797-be5a-3015107a11ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123699/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "a08d14bb-d059-5cc7-a1a8-375af38c60fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123699/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "2d35eb1c-6228-5be6-b4c0-10dd5f8f764b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123699/selection/a17c7bfd1556c549e72b2ad67685fc333175f26ac2a336a4ff04a96a28a6e7f0" :answer/id #uuid "4a1a568c-100d-58a8-bb67-2b2c61335cce" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The sequence diverges." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123699/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1d105b68-3533-5781-a926-8c0c96e958b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123699/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-123699/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-123699/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-123699/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-123699/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-123699/selection/a17c7bfd1556c549e72b2ad67685fc333175f26ac2a336a4ff04a96a28a6e7f0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123699" :question/id #uuid "ca8b6c60-d3e5-5453-9458-79ebc1aabeff" :question/math-academy-id "q-123699" :question/problem "What is the limit of the sequence ${a}_{n}=\\frac{{n}^{2}}{{e}^{n/2}}-1?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for large values of $n,$ we have\n\n$$\nn!≫{e}^{n}≫{n}^{m}≫\\operatorname{ln}⁡(n),\n$$\n\nwhere $≫$ means \"much greater than,\" and $m>0.$\n\nWe calculate the limit of the sequence as $n$ approaches infinity:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n}={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }(\\frac{{n}^{2}}{{e}^{n/2}}-1)=-1+{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{{n}^{2}}{{e}^{n/2}}\n$$\n\nBoth the numerator and denominator approach infinity as $n\\to \\infty .$ However, the denominator is growing much faster than the numerator, and we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{{n}^{2}}{{e}^{n/2}}=0.\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n}=-1+{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{{n}^{2}}{{e}^{n/2}}=-1+0=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sequence converges and its limit is $-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-123699/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "43f839b4-2b0e-5ab5-809a-741747f1016d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123699"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-70781/selection/63079cc748dc757e7a8e5256fd2c9d955e6cf36193b2548b0f6e7b6b72fbf55c" :answer/id #uuid "12c49739-05ab-5796-ad83-a8778a932547" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70781/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "9032cce5-dc4d-55c6-aa9e-1e26837ea8c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70781/selection/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951" :answer/id #uuid "f9f1b7a0-0a0b-57e6-87e4-761b0ca30a9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70781/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "e71f59e8-da7d-549f-9db5-1934ad7bffd6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70781/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "f685487a-e321-540c-ba7a-b0d6cea134fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70781/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f96b5dc3-7d83-5a5a-94b8-fd23d06acd3d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-70781/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-70781/selection/63079cc748dc757e7a8e5256fd2c9d955e6cf36193b2548b0f6e7b6b72fbf55c" "q-70781/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-70781/selection/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951" "q-70781/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-70781/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-70781" :question/id #uuid "553a2492-7880-54fb-8193-a269d45e9e5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-70781" :question/problem "Which of the following values is in the range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/assets/d7984b9098d02bfc2b1e9a422aef919533abce54fbb94117e709c7613b0870a3.png)\n\nNote that:\n\n- The range of the function is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$\n\nTherefore, of the given values, only $y=1$ is in the range of the function." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-70781/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1587e39e-c7bf-5385-b726-a1b497f7c772"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-70781"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-47675/selection/60e712865602c7b754cc04c263111d252dbf5b5d6fef941311ac533c19a75ddb" :answer/id #uuid "60e76c3e-b2e2-5a30-bd0c-5d935a82dc0e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-4$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47675/selection/db48a75ea737230d29e8a4e307051b10fb3f2a183261fb71c846ff91111900fd" :answer/id #uuid "87f95ba7-3a8e-54d7-9060-880ec7bc0934" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-4$ and $x=4$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47675/selection/0f4dd13f4ea79fa9a8d2fa2552ab59e56be4a7d93a738ea8aae511b58b58db23" :answer/id #uuid "ab9d9885-11f8-59ce-94f6-1de0f9b8a353" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-4$, $x=0$ and $x=4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47675/selection/517b13fa7d7411493417798333c215e538be20515774e23158b4c71536604686" :answer/id #uuid "b6947e43-d9f4-5b79-bc3a-e1dbb825a3e8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=0$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47675/selection/c00b423d38fc022695304b5623f8f16d80f952174b860c25dbbf7c6f3e0429ea" :answer/id #uuid "3000dd67-6539-5c32-adce-41e65bb77280" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=4$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47675/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "db81b04a-cbc0-5292-aa6c-ee07d857b021" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-47675/selection/0f4dd13f4ea79fa9a8d2fa2552ab59e56be4a7d93a738ea8aae511b58b58db23" :answer-field/choices ["q-47675/selection/60e712865602c7b754cc04c263111d252dbf5b5d6fef941311ac533c19a75ddb" "q-47675/selection/db48a75ea737230d29e8a4e307051b10fb3f2a183261fb71c846ff91111900fd" "q-47675/selection/0f4dd13f4ea79fa9a8d2fa2552ab59e56be4a7d93a738ea8aae511b58b58db23" "q-47675/selection/517b13fa7d7411493417798333c215e538be20515774e23158b4c71536604686" "q-47675/selection/c00b423d38fc022695304b5623f8f16d80f952174b860c25dbbf7c6f3e0429ea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-47675" :question/id #uuid "3b0f90fb-bc0c-512a-b9f1-eee634aeb642" :question/math-academy-id "q-47675" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/assets/dd8697532367aa85a521d4af3af6f9184e89964f2619ee4dc4ffe84d21877f31.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ whose graph is plotted above. At which points is the function $f(x)$ **not** differentiable?" :question/worked-solution "The function is not differentiable wherever it has a discontinuity, corner, cusp, or vertical tangent.\n\n- At $x=-4$ the function has a jump discontinuity, so it's not differentiable there.\n\n- At $x=0$ the function has a corner, so it's not differentiable there.\n\n- At $x=4$ the function has an infinite discontinuity, so it's not differentiable there.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x=-4$, $x=0$, and $x=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-47675/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7dcbd56f-0fc2-59c5-a016-4272be4734c7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-47675"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-77893/selection/b3ad52392b0dc8e5235a503a1575dcbf1d64bd94300d1aaf710d2724f0fe17df" :answer/id #uuid "dbb62ce0-56fb-510d-877d-6f12819da862" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5x+6y-12=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77893/selection/20ed1d4900a4efc9a54bcfe417da144e20257e8168253ffe0d3990a2789e9328" :answer/id #uuid "44dd6e4f-cda6-58d7-b4d1-716ddcc3df47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6x-5y+12=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77893/selection/60caff7c94940424e5c9f5d2b7e6e65cee081ff93992d3f840374622b45deb70" :answer/id #uuid "2cb4685a-afbb-50e0-afe6-4b2938a0001c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6x+5y+12=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77893/selection/279dc80f74083169b5e92f89537529ebcdaaf25a34af52449711042f01d6e761" :answer/id #uuid "e8c36d31-3476-5948-a639-8c4dc49d7acc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5x-6y+12=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77893/selection/78b451fb09c72a91aed67b8107e52955b98c7e8bae7b3e50662fd5eb99a05f09" :answer/id #uuid "0ee27f95-0c44-5083-bd9e-857f75a2af62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5x-6y-2=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77893/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cd18d463-d93f-53ae-bdbb-266d99b693e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-77893/selection/60caff7c94940424e5c9f5d2b7e6e65cee081ff93992d3f840374622b45deb70" :answer-field/choices ["q-77893/selection/b3ad52392b0dc8e5235a503a1575dcbf1d64bd94300d1aaf710d2724f0fe17df" "q-77893/selection/20ed1d4900a4efc9a54bcfe417da144e20257e8168253ffe0d3990a2789e9328" "q-77893/selection/60caff7c94940424e5c9f5d2b7e6e65cee081ff93992d3f840374622b45deb70" "q-77893/selection/279dc80f74083169b5e92f89537529ebcdaaf25a34af52449711042f01d6e761" "q-77893/selection/78b451fb09c72a91aed67b8107e52955b98c7e8bae7b3e50662fd5eb99a05f09"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-77893" :question/id #uuid "0966918f-fe74-55cf-9f19-d48b021374b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-77893" :question/problem "Consider the line $2x-y-4=0$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the line $2x-y-4=0$ passes through the points $R(0,-4)$ and $S(1,-2)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $R$ and $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 3 \\\\ -12 & -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${R}^{′}(8,-12)$ and ${S}^{′}(3,-6).$\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${R}^{′}$ and ${S}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-12) & =\\frac{-6-(-12)}{3-8}(x-8) \\\\ y+12 & =-\\frac{6}{5}(x-8) \\\\ 5y+60 & =-6x+48 \\\\ 6x+5y+12 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-77893/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15e8730b-c59a-5897-8c83-073b54f517a9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-77893"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
